\"))\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"With both chips populated, the PWM, TACH, SCK, SDA and RST lines are driven or loaded by two MCUs. Output contention can disturb the fan PWM signal and ISP programming, and the fan control behaviour becomes unpredictable. The design may not work as intended.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.55\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist places two microcontrollers, U2 (ATtiny45) and U3 (ATtiny13V), on identical signal nets with no do-not-populate marking, so their PWM, TACH, ISP and POT pins would contend if both were fitted. The other passives, transistor pin assignments and ISP pinout are consistent with a sensible fan-controller design, and the specification does not describe this board, so this verdict rests on general design practice.\"\n}",
